g uncertainty, there is no clear support for the registered expected direction at the approximately 10% meaningfulness scale. I therefore reject H19 and H21 for the registered hypotheses and close those investigations, while recognizing that an opposite direction is not ruled out and would require a new, explicit hypothesis if pursued.\n\nH20, H22, H23, H24, and H25 are decisive positive subgroup-mean tests. H20 gives raw SMARCA4-loss minus non-loss difference about -0.788 in high-Cas9 screens, indicating much stronger SMARCA2 dependency. H22-H24 give raw KEAP1-loss minus KEAP1-retained differences about +0.775, +0.793, and +0.793 for NFE2L2 dependency in STK11-loss, KRAS-wildtype, and adenocarcinoma contexts, respectively; because more negative dependency means stronger dependency, these positive values mean KEAP1-loss cells have markedly weaker NFE2L2 dependency, consistent with the validated reversal already captured by H13. H25 gives raw MSI-high minus non-MSI WRN difference about -0.776 in high-Cas9 screens, indicating much stronger WRN dependency. These effects are enormous relative to the outcome scale and comfortably exceed any plausible 10% meaningfulness criterion even before considering the very narrow 95% intervals.\n\nMultiplicity is still relevant, but I am only accepting effects that are orders of magnitude beyond the noise floor and consistent across related robustness tests. The interaction nulls are not being used to prove absence of all modification; they are simply weak evidence against large effect modification in the tested contexts. The accepted findings remain dataset associations and robustness patterns, not causal claims or externally generalizable biological proof. I request independent validation for H9 because the MSI-high exposed group is the smallest of the accepted main groups and independent replication would strengthen the WRN/MSI-high association without reusing the same discovery cells. H13 already has validation; H7 can be validated later if needed.",
